\begin{lemma}[Regularity at the actual boundary trace]
\label{lem:annular-disk-boundary}
\uses{lem:annular-disk-interior,lem:annular-disk-conformal}
\lean{PoincareMT.M65Boundary.weakDisk_boundary_local_contMDiff,PoincareMT.m65PlateauBoundaryRegularityInput_proved}
The representative is $C^1$ within the closed disk and retains
its continuous weakly monotone trace on the regular Jordan curve.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
Use a holomorphic half-disk chart and straighten the captured
regular target arc. Trace-preserving half-disk replacements give
boundary energy decay. The transverse harmonic equations control
the transverse derivative columns. Conformality determines the
square of the remaining longitudinal column; continuity and the
interior sign choice extend that column through both its zero and
nonzero sets. Integrating the extended differential gives
within-$C^1$ regularity. The local extensions agree on overlaps.
\end{proof}

